{"status":"ready","content":"## Finding the Sample Standard Deviation\r\n\r\n**Step 1: Find the mean**\r\n\r\n$$\\bar{x} = \\frac{1 + (-21) + (-21) + (-18) + 8}{5} = \\frac{-51}{5} = -10.2$$\r\n\r\n**Step 2: Find the squared deviations from the mean**\r\n\r\n- $(1 - (-10.2))^2 = (11.2)^2 = 125.44$\r\n- $(-21 - (-10.2))^2 = (-10.8)^2 = 116.64$\r\n- $(-21 - (-10.2))^2 = (-10.8)^2 = 116.64$\r\n- $(-18 - (-10.2))^2 = (-7.8)^2 = 60.84$\r\n- $(8 - (-10.2))^2 = (18.2)^2 = 331.24$\r\n\r\n**Step 3: Sum the squared deviations**\r\n\r\n$$\\sum = 125.44 + 116.64 + 116.64 + 60.84 + 331.24 = 750.8$$\r\n\r\nConverting to fractions: $\\frac{3754}{5}$\r\n\r\n**Step 4: Divide by (n-1) = 4**\r\n\r\n$$s^2 = \\frac{3754/5}{4} = \\frac{3754}{20} = \\frac{1877}{10}$$\r\n\r\n**Step 5: Take the square root**\r\n\r\n$$s = \\sqrt{\\frac{1877}{10}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{18770}}{10}$$\r\n\r\nChecking if 18770 simplifies: $18770 = 2 \\times 5 \\times 1877$, and 1877 is prime.\r\n\r\n$$s = \\frac{\\sqrt{18770}}{10}$$\r\n\r\n$$\\boxed{\\dfrac{\\sqrt{18770}}{10}}$$\r\n","path":"responses/claude-sonnet-4-6/livebench-070-math.txt","size":932,"mtime":1779367874}